########################Website Run Commands — Command # Meaning#############

Command	Meaning
cd ~/E-commerce-NEXT-APP	#Website ke project folder mein jaana.
ls	                         #Project files aur folders dekhna.
npm install	                 #Project ki required dependencies install karna.
nano .env.local	                 #Environment variables ki file create ya edit karna.
npm run dev	                  #Website ko development mode mein start karna.
npm run build	                  #Production ke liye website build karna.
npm start	                  #Production build ko run karna, agar project mein start script configured hai.
Ctrl + C	                  #Running development server ko stop karna.


####    MongoDB Database Troubleshooting Commands — Ubuntu Linux
1. Check MongoDB Installation
Command	Meaning
mongod --version	Checks the MongoDB server version.
mongosh --version	Checks the MongoDB Shell version.
dpkg -l \| grep -i mongo	Checks installed MongoDB packages.

###########################2. Check and Manage the Database Service
Command	Meaning
sudo systemctl status mongod	Checks whether the MongoDB service is running.
sudo systemctl start mongod	Starts the MongoDB service.
sudo systemctl restart mongod	Restarts the MongoDB service.
sudo systemctl enable mongod	Configures MongoDB to start automatically at boot.
sudo systemctl stop mongod	Stops the MongoDB service.
sudo systemctl daemon-reload	Reloads systemd service configuration files.






############################3. Check Database Errors and Logs

Command	Meaning
sudo journalctl -u mongod -n 50 --no-pager	Displays the latest 50 MongoDB log messages.
sudo journalctl -u mongod -f	Displays MongoDB logs in real time.
##########################4. Check Database Connectivity
Command	Meaning
sudo ss -lntp \| grep 27017	Checks whether a process is listening on MongoDB's default port, 27017.
mongosh "mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017"	Connects to the local MongoDB server.
mongosh --eval 'db.runCommand({ ping: 1 })'	Tests whether MongoDB responds to a ping command.
mongosh --eval 'show dbs'	Lists available databases.


#########################5. Troubleshoot the Next.js Website Database Connection
Command	Meaning
cd ~/E-commerce-NEXT-APP	Opens the project directory.
grep -R "DB_URI" utils	Searches the utils directory for references to the database connection variable.
npm run dev	Starts the Next.js development server.
The project's .env.local file should contain a local MongoDB connection string:
DB_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/ecommerce
